invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_mul.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: table_select loads the one entry its digit names, so the address
  of the load is five bits of the signing nonce, and the cache line it
  touched says which. The value is right, so the vectors, the
  equivalence binary and the proofs all pass, the scan's branch is gone,
  so the branch count falls, and the time does not move with the digit,
  so the t-test passes. The Semgrep rule
  inv-16-p256-wide-no-subscript-by-digit refuses the subscript.

